{
  "annotations": {
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false,
    "readOnlyHint": true,
    "title": "Peek bag samples"
  },
  "description": "Peek up to `count` samples from a recorded bag file as a `SampleResult`: offline, for post-mortem (`peek_dds_samples` and `sample_messages` are live). Formats, by extension: MCAP (`.mcap`), rosbag2 SQLite (`.db3`), ROS 1 (`.bag`). Returns the **first** `count` messages of the topic in recording order, not the last. **Clocks**: `timestamp_ns` is `header.stamp` when the message has a top-level header (`stamp_source` `header`), else the time in the body of `Clock`, `TFMessage` or `Log` (`payload`), else the bag record time (`recorded`); `recorded_ns` is always the record time. Each `payload` carries `_decode_status` (`full` / `partial` / `raw`). `count` defaults to 5, clamped to 50. **Uses the `rosbags` library** and needs the ROS 2 side of the runtime (an error on a DDS-only setup). Mock returns fixtures on canned paths. A bag without embedded definitions (Humble `.db3`) is decoded with those of its recorded distro, or Humble; `note` says which. Arrays over 4096 elements are cut and `note` lists them. **Read-only by architecture**. **Raises an MCP error** when the path does not exist, the topic is not in the bag, or `rosbags` is missing. **Summary and rate**: `LaserScan`, `Odometry`, `Imu`, `Image` and `PointCloud2` samples carry a `summary` of the whole message (other types: null); `rate` gives frequency, interval spread and a `verdict` measured on `recorded_ns` (the bag record time of the returned messages). Use `count` >= 10 (50 above 20 Hz); a multi-publisher topic such as `/tf` reads `erratic` without being broken. **Duration**: takes no lock (in-process file read, so it runs while a ROS 2 or DDS call is busy); the time follows the bag's size and how deep the first samples are.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "properties": {
      "count": {
        "default": 5,
        "description": "Messages to return, default 5, at most 50 (`health_check.max_sample_count`): more is capped to 50, negative raises an error. The result's `count` may be lower.",
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "path": {
        "description": "Bag path: a `.mcap` or `.db3` file or a `rosbag2_*` directory (`peek_bag_samples` also reads ROS 1 `.bag`; `analyze_bag` does not). Existence and format are checked live; mock accepts any well-formed path.",
        "minLength": 1,
        "type": "string"
      },
      "topic": {
        "description": "Fully qualified ROS 2 topic name starting with `/`, e.g. `/cmd_vel`. Segments are letters, digits and underscores (not starting with a digit); anything else is rejected before reaching the `ros2` CLI.",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "path",
      "topic"
    ],
    "type": "object"
  },
